 p,.plan p{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;line-height:1.7}.stat{background:#edf0e8;padding:18px;border-radius:14px;margin-bottom:10px}.stat b{font:400 29px Georgia,serif;display:block}.tile{min-height:165px;text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink)}.num{font-size:10px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.15em;color:#39706f}.tile h3,.plan h3{font:400 24px Georgia,serif;margin:10px 0}.plan{background:var(--deep);color:#fff;border:0}.plan p{color:#cad8dc}.plan a{color:#f3c96b;font-size:11px;font-weight:900}.head{margin:25px 0 12px}.owner{margin-top:25px;background:#e8ecdf}.disclosure{margin-top:20px;color:#68736b;font-size:11px;line-height:1.6}@media(max-width:700px){.intro,.tiles,.plans{grid-template-columns:1fr}.navlinks{display:none}.hero-content{padding:80px 0}.card{padding:21px}}</style><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TouristDestination","name":"Beaver Lake","url":"https://ozartkroost.onrender.com/destinations/beaver-lake","touristType":["Anglers","Boaters","Families","Outdoor travelers"]}</script></head><body><header class="hero"><div class="wrap"><nav class="nav"><a class="logo" href="/">OzarkRoost</a><div class="navlinks"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/listings">Stays</a><a href="/adventures">Adventures</a><a href="/list-your-cabin">List Free</a></div></nav><div class="hero-content"><div class="eyebrow">Flagship destination · Northwest Arkansas Ozarks</div><h1>Beaver Lake</h1><p>Clear water, limestone bluffs, coves, marinas and nearly 500 miles of shoreline make Beaver Lake a natural Ozark playground for fishing, boating, paddling, swimming and camping.</p><a class="btn primary" href="/guides/best-lakes-in-the-ozarks">Explore lake guides →</a><a class="btn ghost" href="/listings">Find a stay</a></div></div></header><main class="wrap main"><section class="intro"><article class="card"><h2>Your water-first Ozarks base</h2><p>Beaver Lake covers about 28,370 acres and has roughly 487 miles of shoreline. Public recreation areas support boating, swimming, camping, hiking and fishing, while cabins, resorts and marinas make multi-day trips easy to build.</p><p>Its location also makes it a powerful hub: pair lake time with Eureka Springs, Bentonville, Rogers or Hobbs State Park–Conservation Area.</p></article><aside class="card"><div class="stat"><b>28,370 ac</b><span>lake surface area</span></div><div class="stat"><b>487 mi</b><span>shoreline</span></div><div class="stat"><b>Water + trails</b><span>easy to combine in one trip</span></div></aside></section><div class="head"><h2>Choose your lake day</h2></div><section class="tiles"><a class="tile" href="/guides/ozarks-fishing-trips"><span class="num">01 · FISH</span><h3>Go fishing</h3><p>Bass, striper, crappie and other species make Beaver a year-round angling destination.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/best-kayaking-in-the-ozarks"><span class="num">02 · PADDLE</span><h3>Paddle a cove</h3><p>Explore quiet water by kayak, canoe or paddleboard and look for sheltered shoreline.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/ozarks-camping"><span class="num">03 · CAMP</span><h3>Camp lakeside</h3><p>Choose a developed recreation area or nearby campground and plan around your launch point.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/best-hiking-ozarks"><span class="num">04 · HIKE</span><h3>Hike Hobbs</h3><p>Connect the lake with ridgelines, hollows and forest trails at Hobbs State Park.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/destinations/eureka-springs"><span class="num">05 · TOWN</span><h3>Add Eureka Springs</h3><p>Turn a lake trip into a full weekend with historic streets, food, caves and local attractions.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/destinations/bentonville"><span class="num">06 · NWA</span><h3>Add Bentonville</h3><p>Mix water with art, food and some of the region's best mountain biking.</p></a></section><div class="head"><h2>Build the trip</h2></div><section class="plans"><article class="plan"><h3>Day on the water</h3><p>Launch early, fish or paddle, swim, then finish with a lakeside meal.</p><a href="/guides/best-kayaking-in-the-ozarks">Plan the water →</a></article><article class="plan"><h3>Lake weekend</h3><p>Book a cabin or campsite, choose two water activities and leave one afternoon open.</p><a href="/listings">Find lodging →</a></article><article class="plan"><h3>Ozark circuit</h3><p>Combine Beaver Lake with Eureka Springs and Bentonville for a bigger regional getaway.</p><a href="/guides/ozarks-weekend-getaway">Build a weekend →</a></article></section><section class="card owner"><h2>Own a Beaver Lake business?</h2><p>Cabins, marinas, guides, restaurants, outfitters and experiences can claim a founding destination listing.</p><a class="btn primary" href="/list-your-cabin">Claim a free founding spot →</a></section><div class="disclosure">OzarkRoost is an independent travel directory. Lake levels, ramps, weather, regulations and operating schedules can change. Verify current information before launch or travel.</div></main></body></html>